WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:15.848
Miss Shelly called.

2
00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:19.251
It was Talk Like a Pirate Day at Kids Central.

3
00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.113
Everyone was dressed up.

4
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.835
"Yo, ho, ho!"

5
00:00:24.616 --> 00:00:26.237
Nina wore a purple eye patch.

6
00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:29.680
Bobby had made his cast look like a peg leg.

7
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:33.478
"Hey, Ethan, what's on your shoulder?"

8
00:00:33.758 --> 00:00:34.358
he asked.

9
00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:37.041
"A parrot, of course!"

10
00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:38.342
Ethan replied.

11
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:41.264
Jason waved a rubber sword.

12
00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:43.986
"Shiver me timbers!"

13
00:00:45.127 --> 00:00:48.030
"I hope you pirates are hungry," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.912
"We're having a pirate feast."

15
00:00:52.753 --> 00:00:53.914
"What are we making?"

16
00:00:54.295 --> 00:00:55.095
Nina asked.

17
00:00:56.496 --> 00:01:00.680
"Pirate peg legs and sea sauce," Miss Shelly said.

18
00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:04.654
"I hope we're not eating my peg leg!"

19
00:01:04.974 --> 00:01:05.754
Bobby said.

20
00:01:06.895 --> 00:01:07.956
Miss Shelly laughed.

21
00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:10.617
"Don't worry.

22
00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:13.919
We're making fish sticks with tartar sauce."

23
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.140
She looked around.

24
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.701
"Where's Izzie?"

25
00:01:17.721 --> 00:01:23.084
"Here." Izzie entered the gym and sat down.

26
00:01:24.324 --> 00:01:25.285
She didn't look happy.

27
00:01:26.065 --> 00:01:27.766
And she wasn't dressed like a pirate.

28
00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:29.367
"What's up, Izzie?"

29
00:01:29.727 --> 00:01:30.568
Jason asked.

30
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.801
"I don't want to be a pirate," Izzie said.

31
00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:38.363
"You don't have to be a pirate," Miss Shelly said.

32
00:01:38.383 --> 00:01:41.944
"But everyone has to help with making our snack.

33
00:01:42.765 --> 00:01:45.166
We'll make the pirate peg legs first."

34
00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:47.847
"I'll preheat the oven!"

35
00:01:48.147 --> 00:01:48.967
Jason said.

36
00:01:48.987 --> 00:01:53.969
Nina followed the directions on the board.

37
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:57.591
"First, we beat two eggs.

38
00:01:59.572 --> 00:02:03.073
Then, we pour bread crumbs into a shallow bowl."

39
00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:09.915
"Next, we dip the pieces of fish in the eggs," Jason read.

40
00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:13.996
"Then into the bread crumbs," Bobby added.

41
00:02:14.016 --> 00:02:18.337
"Remember to use a fork for dipping," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:02:19.557 --> 00:02:22.878
The kids took turns dipping the fish into the eggs and bread crumbs.

43
00:02:22.898 --> 00:02:28.740
"Now we put the fish on a tray," Bobby said.

44
00:02:33.396 --> 00:02:36.037
Jason carefully slid the tray into the toaster oven.

45
00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.980
Izzie sat at a table, still looking glum.

46
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.680
Miss Shelly went over.

47
00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.222
"What's bothering you, Izzie?"

48
00:02:46.242 --> 00:02:50.603
"I don't like Talk Like a Pirate Day," Izzie said.

49
00:02:50.623 --> 00:02:54.205
"I don't want to talk like a boy."

50
00:02:54.285 --> 00:02:58.507
"There were female pirates too," Miss Shelly said.

51
00:02:58.527 --> 00:03:01.288
"No way," Jason said.

52
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.441
"The pirates in my video game say girls are bad luck on a ship!"

53
00:03:06.981 --> 00:03:09.942
"Well, they never met Anne Bonny and Mary Read."

54
00:03:11.043 --> 00:03:12.703
Miss Shelly handed Izzie a book.

55
00:03:12.723 --> 00:03:16.964
"These women are two of history's fiercest pirates."

56
00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:20.285
"Really?" Izzie grinned.

57
00:03:20.305 --> 00:03:26.207
"Cool!" Nina took off her purple eye patch.

58
00:03:26.227 --> 00:03:32.896
"Do you want to wear my eye patch, Izzie?"

59
00:03:32.956 --> 00:03:34.397
"Aye!" Izzie laughed.

60
00:03:34.417 --> 00:03:36.277
"Thanks, Nina.

61
00:03:36.897 --> 00:03:38.858
Can we make the sea sauce now?"

62
00:03:40.038 --> 00:03:41.039
Miss Shelly nodded.

63
00:03:41.059 --> 00:03:43.819
"Let's turn the fish sticks first."

64
00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.961
The kids started making the sauce.

65
00:03:49.201 --> 00:03:53.202
"We add one cup of mayonnaise to a medium bowl," Bobby read.

66
00:03:53.222 --> 00:03:59.444
"Now we need six tablespoons of chopped sweet pickles," Jason said.

67
00:04:00.648 --> 00:04:03.369
"Squeeze one lemon for juice," Ethan said.

68
00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:05.330
"Then mix!"

69
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:06.451
Izzie said.

70
00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:10.432
The kids took turns measuring, squeezing, and mixing.

71
00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.075
Ding! The timer rang.

72
00:04:22.538 --> 00:04:24.518
Our pirate peg legs are ready!"

73
00:04:24.819 --> 00:04:25.519
Bobby said.

74
00:04:26.659 --> 00:04:27.660
Everyone sat down.

75
00:04:29.385 --> 00:04:31.650
Izzie raised her water bottle to make a toast.

76
00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:35.278
"These peg legs look delicious.

77
00:04:36.461 --> 00:04:37.403
Eat up, pirates!"
